All 15 tests pass. Here's what was fixed across the 3 modules:

**`src/auth.py`** — 2 bugs
- `has_permission` line 8: case-sensitive `in` check → case-insensitive comparison via `.lower()`
- `is_admin_or_owner` line 14: `and` → `or` (admin *or* owner should grant access, not both)

**`src/inventory.py`** — 4 bugs
- `__init__` line 13: mutable default `{}` shared across instances → `None` default with fresh `dict(initial)` per call
- `add` line 21: `self._stock[sku] = qty` overwrites → `self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty` accumulates
- `reserve` line 27: `>=` → `>` (reserving exactly available stock should succeed)
- `release` line 35: no negative check → raises `ValueError` when releasing more than reserved

**`src/text_utils.py`** — 2 bugs
- `slugify` line 18: no lowercasing → `char.lower()` on each character
- `slugify` line 29: `replace("--", "-")` only handles double dashes → `re.sub(r"-+", "-")` collapses any run
- `truncate` line 37: `text[:max_len] + suffix` exceeds max_len → `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix` fits suffix inside the limit
